      "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6a47076bba67319767cc732cc3b68c5b4eb4bc43.001.1",
      "event": "High Surf Advisory",
      "severity": "Minor",
      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 11 at 3:43PM HST until November 12 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH AND WEST FACING SHORES OF NIIHAU\nKAUAI OAHU MOLOKAI AND NORTH FACING SHORES OF MAUI...\n\n.Surf heights has begun to rise quickly this afternoon and is\nexpected to peak late tonight through early Thursday at near-\nwarning level surf. Surf is expected to start falling below\nadvisory levels by Thursday night.\n\n* WHAT...For north-facing shores, surf rising through the evening,\nand peaking at 18 to 24 feet late tonight and Thursday morning,\nthen diminishing through Thursday. For west- facing shores, surf\npeaking at 14 to 18 feet late tonight, then diminishing through\nThursday.\n\n* WHERE...North and west facing shores of Niihau, Kauai, Oahu,\nMolokai and north facing shores of Maui.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM HST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
      "instruction": "Heed all advice from ocean safety officials. When in doubt, don't\ngo out.",
      "areaDesc": "Niihau; Waianae Coast; Oahu North Shore; Maui Windward West; Kauai North; Molokai Windward; Molokai North; Molokai West; Maui Central Valley North; Windward Haleakala",
